  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRA ACM Pakistan 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As result of unprecedented seasonal monsoon rains in Pakistan nearly a third of the country is flooded. According to Pakistan&apos;s National Disaster Management Authority (NDMA) as of September 8 there are almost 1,400 fatal casualties. 33 million people are affected across the country, amongst others in the Sindh province. Their main concern is to find shelter (almost 1,5M houses are damaged), to have food to eat and water to drink and to have functional sanitary facilities (http://cms.ndma.gov.pk/storage/app/public/situation-reports/September2022/8HRXtyqMDEPTchwNDOw0.pdf). 
Within Sindh the Manchar Lake, in the north of the Jamshoro distict, has broken through its water containing dams. Equally affected is nearby Dadu district (https://reliefweb.int/report/pakistan/early-needs-identification-flood-disaster-sindh-pakistan . A rapid needs assessment as of September 3rd 2022 by local NGO Rural Education and Economic Development Society (REEDS) (https://reedspak.org/rapid-need-assessment-reports/) indicates that in Dadu 818,000 people are affected, with 42,000 in temporary relief camps as 39,000 houses are damaged. In Jamshoro district 36,000 people are affected, almost all of them now in refuge in camps without houses. Even the camps are now affected, with demolished latrines resulting in open defacation and subsequent potential water borne diseases. Tarpaulins, NFIs for WASH and food are needed urgently. On the longer run food assistance should compensate loss in livestock (drowned) and crops (flooded). 
The Pakistani government thusfar has provided lots of assistance (https://www.pdma.gos.pk/new/Docs/SITREP_03-09-2022.pdf) but gaps remain high in Jamshoro and Dadu, especially in Shelter/NFIs and FSL. 
Cordaid&apos;s intervention jumps into the identified gaps, addressing needs of 3,500 most affected and vulnerable people in Dadu and Jamshoro districts.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cordaid proposes an MPC and WASH intervention to address needs of 25,000 floods affected people in Jamshoro and Dadu districts, in coordination with targeted communities.
Provision of MPC for 1000 flood affected families of district Jamshoroo and Dadu
Provision of Water and Sanitation facilities for and Hygiene material for 1000 families of targeted UCs of district Jamshoroo and Dadu in Sindh province of Pakistan.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Flood hit most vulnerable women, children, elderly, people with special needs, transgenders and religious minorities receive life assistance support.</narrative>
  </description>
